      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It's not a solution but it would generate useful data points across multiple instances. Surviving in a world with a crash wouldn't flag anyone, consistently surviving in a world with crashes would. \nThis sort of information can be combined with other information to create an automated system to flag accounts for review. The specifics of the system should not be made public to avoid people gaming it. \nAlso, initial bans should be temporary, and IP data of flagged and banned users should be tracked and used to IP ban people who are creating multiple accounts.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
